  "notes": "{突|つ}く means to poke or thrust with a forward motion. It is also used for propping or leaning body parts on a surface.\n\nTRANSITIVITY:\n- Type: ⟦{他動詞|たどうし}→他動詞：10418_tadoushi⟧ (transitive)\n\nCOMMON EXPRESSIONS:\n- ⟦{嘘|うそ}をつく→嘘をつく：21763_usowotsuku⟧: to tell a lie\n- ⟦{肘|ひじ}をつく→肘をつく：22275_hijiwotsuku⟧: to put one's elbows (on a table)\n- ⟦{杖|つえ}→杖：12862_tsue⟧⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧つく: to use a cane\n- ⟦{膝|ひざ}→膝：00940_hiza⟧⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧つく: to kneel (put one's knees to the ground)\n- {溜|た}め{息|いき}⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧つく: to sigh\n\nNOTE: Many of these expressions are commonly written in kana (つく) rather than with the kanji {突|つ}く.\n\nWATCH OUT:\n- ⟦{付|つ}く→付く：01960_tsuku⟧: to be attached, to stick\n- ⟦{着|つ}く→着く：00680_tsuku⟧: to arrive\n- ⟦{就|つ}く→就く：10123_tsuku⟧: to take up (a position)",
